play vs. Bucs, Dan Campbell says","description":"Lions coach Dan Campbell says he expects Alim McNeill to return from a knee injury and play Monday against the Buccaneers.","published":"2025-10-16T17:01:06.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/46603254/lions-alim-mcneill-expected-play-vs-bucs-dan-campbell-says","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Lions' Alim McNeill back practicing after December ACL injury","description":"The Lions' standout defensive tackle is back practicing after a December ACL injury.","published":"2025-10-03T13:46:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/46467560/detroit-lions-nfl-dt-alim-mcneill-back-practicing-december-acl-injury","type":"Story","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2025 Pro Bowl roster snubs: Who should be an NFL all-star?","description":"No initial Pro Bowl roster is perfect, and we identified the best players, such as A.J. Brown and Baker Mayfield, who didn't get their names called on Thursday.","published":"2025-01-02T17:24:54.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/insider/story/_/id/43253011/2025-nfl-pro-bowl-roster-snubs-aj-brown-baker-mayfield","type":"Story","byline":"Ben Solak and Seth Walder","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Lions' David Montgomery, Alim McNeill out for rest of season","description":"Lions running back David Montgomery sustained a sprained MCL, defensive tackle Alim McNeill tore his ACL and cornerback Carlton Davis III sustained a fractured jaw.","published":"2024-12-16T22:04:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/43004551/sources-lions-starting-dt-alim-mcneill-torn-acl","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Lions' Dorsey out for year; DT McNeill, CB Davis likely done too","description":"The Lions lost three key contributors to likely season-ending injuries in CB Khalil Dorsey, DT Alim McNeill and CB Carlton Davis.","published":"2024-12-16T02:56:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/42991102/lions-dorsey-year-dt-mcneill-cb-davis-likely-done-too","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Lions extend Alim McNeill for 4 years; $55M guaranteed, source says","description":"The Lions and DT Alim McNeill agreed to a four-year extension worth $97 million, including $55 million guaranteed, a source confirmed to ESPN.","published":"2024-10-16T12:47:26.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/41818707/lions-extend-alim-mcneill-4-years-55m-guaranteed-source-says","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Lions place DT Alim McNeill on IR due to knee sprain","description":"The Lions placed starting defensive tackle Alim McNeill on injured reserve Tuesday due to a knee sprain.","published":"2023-12-06T12:11:42.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/39049582/lions-place-dt-alim-mcneill-ir-due-knee-sprain","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ranking the top 25 NFL prospects in 2022: Rhamondre Stevenson and the under-the-radar young players who could break out","description":"Football Outsiders unveils its annual list of the league's best and brightest players ... who have barely played.","published":"2022-07-31T10:44:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/insider/story/_/id/34302755/ranking-top-25-nfl-prospects-2022-rhamondre-stevenson-the-radar-young-players-break-out","type":"Story","byline":"Rivers McCown","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Alim McNeill","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alim_McNeill","description":"American football player (born 2000)","touched":"2026-11-24T10:44:39Z","intro":"Alim McNeill (born May 11, 2000) is an American professional football defensive tackle for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the NC State Wolfpack, and was selected by the Lions in the third round of the 2021 NFL draft.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"McNeill attended Jesse O. Sanderson High School in Raleigh, North Carolina. He played linebacker and running back in high school. McNeill committed to North Carolina State University to play college football. He also played baseball in high school."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"McNeill played at NC State from 2018 to 2020. During his career, he had 77 tackles, 10 sacks, one interception and one touchdown. As a junior, he was named an All-American by The Athletic and Pro Football Focus as well as earning All-ACC honors. After that season, he entered the 2021 NFL draft."},{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"McNeill was drafted 72nd overall by the Detroit Lions in the third round of the 2021 NFL draft. He signed his four-year rookie contract on May 13, 2021.\nMcNeill entered the 2023 season as the Lions starting defensive tackle. In Week 8, he recorded two sacks, his first career multi-sack game, and a pass deflection in a 26–14 win over the Las Vegas Raiders. He suffered a knee injury in Week 13 and was placed on injured reserve on December 5, 2023. He was activated on January 6, 2024.\nOn October 15, 2024, McNeill signed a four-year, $97 million contract extension with the Lions. In Week 6's 47–9 victory over the Dallas Cowboys, McNeill recorded two sacks. In Week 15, McNeill tore his ACL in the 48–42 loss to the Buffalo Bills, ending his season. Prior to the injury, McNeill recorded 25 tackles, 3.5 sacks, seven tackles for loss, and seven quarterback hits.\nAfter spending the first six weeks of the season on the PUP list, McNeill was activated for his season debut on October 20, 2025."}],"wikidataId":"Q104450726","social":{}},"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4361662","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/M/McNeAl00.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/alim-mcneill/76996","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/alim-mcneill/9536","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alim_McNeill"},"insights":["Ranks 3rd of 116 qualified interior defensive linemen in defensive snap share.","Ranks 3rd of 85 qualified interior defensive linemen in sacks.","On the field for 77% of Detroit’s defensive snaps this season.","2026 cap number of $29.0M is the 2nd-largest on the roster.","Under contract through 2028."]}